  "description_snippet": "Resources from file:/// do not define a Content-Type, hence, a malicious page can load any local resource as CSS and it will be interpreted as such, independently of the MIME type. This allows to exfiltrate data from cross-origin local files via a CSS injection. This is a small variation of @filedes"
